cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, code or results, please cite it as below."
title: "When Should AI Assist the Assessor? A Philippine Higher-Education Benchmark of Failure Containment, Control Allocation, and Human Verification Burden"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Lambitco
    given-names: Bea Charmelyn T.
    affiliation: "AI for Asia Fellowship 2026 (Philippines)"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of 24 assessment-support cases built from the published rules of nine Philippine
  higher-education institutions (90 scoring criteria), with frozen prompts, answer keys, four
  deterministic release checks, analysis code and aggregate results comparing direct and
  check-controlled release of AI answers, plus human checking time, independent reviewer
  agreement, an AI-judge cross-check and exploratory extensions.
keywords:
  - assessment
  - higher education
  - Philippines
  - large language models
  - human oversight
  - benchmark
  - release controls
notes: "Code is licensed under MIT (see LICENSE); cases, answer keys, documentation and results under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-CONTENT). Quoted policy excerpts remain under their owners' terms."
